<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African rand hits 4.60 vs dlr, two-month high.</title>
<headline>S.African rand hits 4.60 vs dlr, two-month high.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South African rand hit its strongest level in two months against the dollar on Monday, as dealers bid the currency down to 4.60 against the U.S. unit.  </p>
<p>The rand was quoted at 4.5985/6035 at 0805 GMT.  </p>
<p>Dealers said the rand was being buoyed by a market awash with dollars, fuelled by early dollar selling by local speculators.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
